=================== 1. THE POSITION (gradient qp 40, port/C) ===============

  ratio per cell = median of 25 paired per-round ratios; [p25, p75] beside the
  512 cell; slope ratio from the least-squares fit ms = intercept + slope*px
  over the byte-identical sizes. EVERY cell ident=Y unless marked N.

  preset 8         64      128     256     512 [p25,p75]      slope    intercept port / C
  still          0.409   0.864   1.691   1.854 [1.811,1.912]  1.99x     0.031 ms /  0.385 ms
  videokey       0.727   1.281   1.892   1.805 [1.765,1.879]  1.91x    -0.754 ms /  0.146 ms
  inter          1.319   1.621   2.214   2.198 [2.172,2.290]  2.25x    -0.641 ms /  0.192 ms

  preset 2
  still          1.520   1.698   1.751   1.937 [1.856,2.037]  1.98x    46.150 ms / 30.454 ms
  videokey       1.662   1.756   1.754   1.898 [1.843,1.919]  1.91x    40.945 ms / 27.864 ms
  inter          1.845   1.830   1.811  (1.987 N, excluded)   1.81x*  -12.624 ms / -7.317 ms   (*3-size fit)

  preset 6
  still          0.878   1.372   1.679   1.888 [1.787,1.925]  1.88x     0.687 ms /  0.898 ms
  videokey       1.025   1.569   1.721   1.955 [1.900,1.991]  1.99x     1.302 ms /  2.111 ms
  inter          1.475   1.890   1.997   2.332 [2.237,2.377]  2.36x     1.003 ms /  1.928 ms

  Slopes (ms/MP), port / C:
    still     p8  46.2039 /  23.2323    p2 1820.5643 /  918.2591    p6 140.7615 /  74.9033
    videokey  p8 200.5278 / 105.1891    p2 3590.9214 / 1882.3774    p6 438.5833 / 220.0585
    inter     p8 268.7673 / 119.2947    p2 6049.3084 / 3347.1147    p6 589.3731 / 249.3398

  Absolute ms at 512x512, port / C (medians):
    still     p8 12.095 / 6.469    p2  508.273 / 261.633    p6  37.219 / 20.286
    videokey  p8 52.067 / 27.934   p2  962.488 / 508.541    p6 115.451 / 59.067
    inter     p8 70.230 / 31.717   p2 1072.888 / 540.863(N) p6 155.031 / 66.719

WHAT THE TABLE SAYS, AND WHAT IT DOES NOT.

  * Against the 1.25x goal every slope FAILS, 1.81x-2.36x. The worst arm on
    this host is inter p6 (2.36x), and inter is the only arm whose ratio is
    still rising at 512 on every preset.
  * THE INTERCEPT IS A SEPARATE QUANTITY, per the sweep rule, and here it
    cuts both ways. On p6/p8 C carries a real positive fixed per-frame cost
    (still p8 0.385 ms, p6 0.898 ms) where the port's is ~0, so the port is
    FASTER than C at 64x64 on still p8 (0.41x) and p6 (0.88x) and at parity
    on videokey p6 64 (1.03x). At p2 there is NO such crossover: 64x64 reads
    1.52x-1.85x, and the p2 fits put tens of ms of intercept on BOTH sides --
    that is the straight line failing on a cost/px that falls ~2.6x from 64
    to 512 at p2 (20.671 ms at 64x64 = ~5 us/px vs ~1.9 us/px at 512), not a
    fixed cost. Read the p2 cells, not the p2 intercepts.
  * THE INTER FRAME'S OWN COST, by the harness's differencing method (N=2
    minus N=1, medians of the same session): gradient 512 p8 port 70.230 -
    52.067 = 18.16 ms vs C 31.717 - 27.934 = 3.78 ms; p6 155.031 - 115.451 =
    39.58 ms vs 66.719 - 59.067 = 7.65 ms; photo p6 271.069 - 248.843 = 22.23
    ms vs 163.884 - 160.121 = 3.76 ms. The port side is resolved (its two
    cells' p25/p75 half-widths are ~1-2 ms); the C side is NOT resolved
    beyond "a few ms" (C videokey 512 p8 [27.095, 28.623], inter [30.775,
    32.176]). So: the inter frame ALONE is roughly 4-6x C on this box, under
    a 2.2x whole-sequence ratio. Subtraction of measurements, not a
    projection.

