  TWO CELLS ARE BYTE FINDINGS, NOT RESULTS -- the arm10 findings re-observed
  on x86 at 7ec5b5572, plus one change:
    * photo 512 p2 VIDEOKEY ident=N (re-run by hand: frame 0 port 117,173 B
      vs C 117,167 B). Still-mode p2 and videokey p6 on the same image ARE
      identical. Same cell arm10 flagged; unchanged.
    * photo 512 p2 INTER now ENCODES (25/25 rounds, zero ERR) where arm10
      recorded a clean REFUSAL -- the global-motion landing (INTER-ENCODE-
      PLAN §1z41-42) lifted it. It is ident=N by frame 0 (the videokey
      finding above); frame 1 then reads 32 vs 37 B, which says nothing on
      its own since it predicts from a different reconstruction.

=================== 3. A NEW BYTE FINDING ON THE SYNTHETIC ARM =============

  gradient 512x512 qp40 p2 INTER is ident=N: frame 0 IDENTICAL (19,211 B on
  both sides), FRAME 1 DIFFERS, port 37 B vs C 38 B. 512 lies outside the
  {16,64,128,256} x {p0,p2,p3,p4} band §1z41 closed, so this is a previously
  UNOBSERVED cell, not a regression claim. One byte on the inter frame is the
  same shape as the 96-cell grid's `diag 128x128 q20 p8` F1DIFF. Debugger:
  `tools/identity_diff_inter.sh 512 512 40 2 gradient` with the inter env
  exported (see WORKING-ON-THIS.md §5). Excluded from the p2 inter fit, which
  is therefore a 3-size fit (64/128/256) and reads 1.81x.

=================== 4. SAME-BINARY CONTROLS, AND THE JITTER ================

  tools/perf_ab.sh, port perf_encode vs a byte-identical copy of itself, 21
  interleaved rounds, this session, this box (ONE s5cmd live throughout):

    gradient 64  p8   0.9940  [0.853, 1.096]   13 of 21 rounds outside +-5 %  (0.648 .. 1.291)
    gradient 512 p8   0.9967  [0.938, 1.046]   12 of 21 rounds outside +-5 %  (0.918 .. 1.131)
    photo    512 p2   1.0031  [0.986, 1.019]
    photo    512 p6   0.9986  [0.969, 1.008]

  The 0.3-0.6 % floor bias against the candidate slot is the one every other
  host shows. What is NEW is the per-round spread: +-5 % at p25/p75 on a
  12 ms gradient cell, against +-0.4 % on the Mac. Two causes are confounded
  and were NOT separated -- WSL2's hypervisor scheduling, and the sibling
  lane's s5cmd sync(s) (pids 42382 then also 71978, ~15-20 % of a thread
  each, from ~/work/zenfuzz-farm/triage-crashes.sh) that ran the whole
  session and were not killed because they were another lane's live work.
  The second run (p26) was launched with one still live, so no clean
  control exists in this record. Consequences for reading it:
    * The 2x-class position ratios are far outside the jitter. They stand.
    * The long photo cells average it out (control +-2 %); the photo p2/p6
      ratios are good to about +-2 %.
    * A sub-5 % per-cell claim on a short gradient cell from this box needs
      its own control and more than 21 rounds; nothing under ~1 % should be
      claimed from this box at all. perf_ab.sh chunk-sized A/Bs belong on
      the Mac or r7900x, not here, until a clean control is measured.
  Loadavg (1-min) stayed in 1.4-3.9 across every arm (threshold for discard
  ~6; nothing discarded); MemAvailable 18.1-22.2 GiB of 23; swap 0 used.
  Per-arm snapshots: perf_2026-09-05-lilith1-quiet.txt and -p26-quiet.txt.

=================== 5. HOST FACTS THAT CONTRADICT WHAT WAS ASSUMED =========

  * `/usr/bin/perf` on lilith is Ubuntu's version-dispatch wrapper and the
    backing `linux-tools-6.18.33.2-microsoft-standard-WSL2` binary does not
    exist: `perf stat` cannot run. No hardware counters on this box.
  * valgrind is 3.18.1 and cannot execute AVX-512, which C's oracle here
    actually uses (ENABLE_AVX512=ON). Neither Ir nor cycles for C's real
    kernels are obtainable on this box. The cycle-vs-Ir story stays on r7900x.
  * `cmake` on the cargo-only PATH is 3.22.1; the 4.2.1 that configured
    cbuild-static is ~/.local/bin (pip). Harmless, recorded so nobody
    "fixes" it.
  * ~/work/zen/scripts/run-heavy (a symlink into ~/work/claudehints) still
    describes this box as "58 GiB WSL2, 28 cores" and defaults --mem to 24G,
    which is above this VM's whole RAM. Not edited (another repo); always
    pass --mem here.
  * The user-level CLAUDE.md figure for this box was corrected to 23 GiB +
    8 GB swap during this session (coordinator); the run used --mem 12G.

=================== HOW TO RE-RUN IT =======================================

  export PATH="$HOME/.cargo/bin:$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH"
  cd ~/work/zen/zenav1-svt/rust
  ~/work/zen/scripts/run-heavy --mem 12G --jobs 8 -- env -u RUSTFLAGS \
      cargo build --release -p zenav1-svt --example perf_encode --example identity_run
  ~/work/zen/scripts/run-heavy --mem 12G --jobs 8 -- tools/perf_c_encode/build.sh
  # photo yuv (verify sha256 88142a48...3ca4a72f):
  ./target/release/examples/identity_run crop:<corpus>/CID22/CID22-512/training/3571065.png \
      512 512 40 8 ~/tmp/pos-lilith/yuv/photo_cid
  # the six arms + controls, un-niced, with the quiet sampler:
  POS_AGENT=<your-id> PERF_ROUNDS=25 tools/perf_position.sh <suffix> ~/tmp/pos-lilith/yuv/photo_cid.yuv
  # gradient p2/p6 as a second pass:
  POS_GRAD_PRESETS="2 6" POS_ARMS="still videokey inter" tools/perf_position.sh <suffix>-p26 <same.yuv>
  Re-claim <repo>/.workongoing afterwards (the driver leaves it reading DONE).

=================== NOT ESTABLISHED ========================================
  * ATTRIBUTION to any landing. A position run resolves nothing per chunk.
  * The AVX-512 share of the gap (C has it; the port had none at 7ec5b5572,
    and 373243b7's single-kernel tier is not in this record).
  * The aarch64 position on THIS tree -- arm10 is still the Mac's last word
    and it is at 41e5d8f1.
  * Any size above 512, any content but gradient and photo_cid, any qp but 40.
  * A clean same-binary control with no sibling job on the box.
